### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@idempotencyKey = {{$guid}}

### 1. Place Order (Happy Path - Returns 202 Accepted)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "customerId": "019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "lines": [
    {
      "productId": "019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 2. Replay Same Order (Idempotency Test - Returns cached 202 with Idempotent-Replayed: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "customerId": "019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "lines": [
    {
      "productId": "019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 3. Place Order without Idempotency-Key (Rejection - Returns 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "lines": [
    {
      "productId": "019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 4. Query Order by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/019488a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### 5. Query All Orders (Paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=1&pageSize=10 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json
